    "claim": "every closed unit square contained in the closed container [0, s]^2, at every centre and every angle, contains points of total weight >= 1",
    "argument": "concentric shrink: a packing of n unit squares in a container of side s' < s, rescaled by s/s' > 1, gives n squares each strictly containing a concentric closed unit square; those have pairwise disjoint interiors, so no point is counted twice and n <= total_weight < n is a contradiction",
